{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Behold, we perish.</b> It is enough for us that we perish and are lost, and behold, all who draw near to the dwelling of HaShem will die. And the duplication of drawing near that he mentioned — drawing near after drawing near — is to say: whoever draws nearer to the Tent more than his fellow will die the death of the burned ones, and would that we were doomed to perish. Then the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Aaron that He appointed him prince over the tribe of Levi, to warn that the Levites not cause Israel to stumble." "<b>And it is fitting</b> to interpret 'Behold, we perish' — 'we are lost, we are all lost,' for Scripture explained the three punishments brought about in this controversy: the swallowing, the burning, and the plague, as I have already explained. And he says: הן גוענו — by the burning; אבדנו — by the swallowing, as it is written, ויאבדו מתוך הקהל; כלנו אבדנו — by the plague, for those who died in the plague were fourteen thousand and seven hundred. And so Onkelos translated: הא מננא קטלת חרבא הא מננא בלעת ארעא הא מננא דמיתו במותנא — the translation of גוענו being קטלת חרבא, and it is a designation for the fire that went forth from before HaShem, which is the attribute of justice; and so the sword of the Holy One, blessed be He, is the attribute of His justice, in the manner of what is said (Isaiah 27:1): ״יפקוד ה׳ בחרבו הקשה וגו׳״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:41.985353630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}